Description: pvr: report 8 color attachments
 maxColorAttachments and maxFragmentOutputAttachments are literals of 4 and
 maxFragmentCombinedOutputResources is 4, the Vulkan 1.0 minimums set by
 a22ad99bdd2 ("pvr: set device features/props/extensions to Vulkan 1.0
 minimums (unless implemented)"). Before that commit the driver reported
 PVR_MAX_COLOR_ATTACHMENTS (8, PVR_NUM_PBE_EMIT_REGS in rogue_hw_defs.h) and
 the sum of color attachments, storage buffers and storage images per stage.
 The hardware has 8 PBE emits per tile: pbestate.xml STATE_WORD1 mrt_index is
 3 bits, kmd_stream.xml CMD_FRAG pbe_word holds 8 x 3 PBE register words.
 .
 On cores without eight_output_registers, such as BXM-4-64, the 4 output
 registers hold one pixel of up to 128 bits (pbestate.xml SOURCE_POS
 START_BIT0..96) and further attachments go to up to 7 tile buffers
 (PVR_MAX_TILE_BUFFER_COUNT). All paths for these exist: allocation for
 render passes and dynamic rendering (pvr_surface_alloc_color_storage(),
 pvr_alloc_mrt()), fragment shader stores (trans_store_output() in
 pco_trans_nir.c), load ops, clears, the end of tile program
 (pvr_usc_eot()), and for partial renders the SPM end of tile program with
 one emit for the output registers and one per tile buffer
 (pvr_arch_spm_init_eot_state(), d1f2ad17dd6 "pvr: Add missing support for
 tile buffers to SPM EOT programs") and the SPM background load
 (pvr_uscgen_spm_load(), up to 7 tile buffers). The "Add support for tile
 buffers in EOT" finishme is in the eight_output_registers branch only. Each
 attachment takes at most 4 dwords, and an attachment only opens a new tile
 buffer when it fits into none of the existing ones, so 8 attachments always
 fit into the output registers and 7 tile buffers; the render pass fallback
 with z replication needs the previous patch.
 .
 Report PVR_MAX_COLOR_ATTACHMENTS for maxColorAttachments and
 maxFragmentOutputAttachments, and maxFragmentCombinedOutputResources as
 color attachments plus storage buffers and storage images per stage. zink
 takes PIPE_CAP max_render_targets and with it GL_MAX_DRAW_BUFFERS from
 maxColorAttachments.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
